    "nuScenes intensity (0-255) is overwritten with 1.0 for every point, because every CARLA training scan has intensity exactly 1.0. xyz-only runs never read the column.",
    "GT follows the CARLA test protocol: a car counts only if num_lidar_pts >= 5 and it lies within 50 m of the sensor (bbox_3d_isvalid). Other cars are ignored as GT, so detections on them count as false positives, exactly as in the CARLA pkl where they were removed.",
    "Scans are single-sweep keyframes from trainval blobs 01+02, scenes from both the official train (5,512 scans) and val (1,231 scans) splits; no model saw nuScenes during training.",
    "carla_test holds the same run/epoch on the CARLA test split (work_dirs/eval_carla_test). drop_pp = (nuScenes - CARLA) * 100; retained_pct = nuScenes / CARLA * 100."
